    "title": "pandas.IntervalIndex.to_tuples — pandas 2.1.4 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.IntervalIndex.to_tuples#\n\n- \nIntervalIndex.to_tuples(**args* ,***kwargs* )[source]#\n- Return an ndarray (if self is IntervalArray) or Index (if self is IntervalIndex) of tuples of the form (left, right). \n  - Parameters:\n    - **na_tuple** bool, default True\n    - If `True` , return`NA` as a tuple`(nan, nan)` . If`False` ,\njust return`NA` as`nan` .\n  - Returns:\n    - tuples: ndarray (if self is IntervalArray) or Index (if self is IntervalIndex)\n Examples For `pandas.IntervalArray` :>>> idx = pd.arrays.IntervalArray.from_tuples([(0, 1), (1, 2)]) >>> idx <IntervalArray> [(0, 1], (1, 2]] Length: 2, dtype: interval[int64, right] >>> idx.to_tuples() array([(0, 1), (1, 2)], dtype=object) For `pandas.IntervalIndex` :>>> idx = pd.interval_range(start=0, end=2) >>> idx IntervalIndex([(0, 1], (1, 2]], dtype='interval[int64, right]') >>> idx.to_tuples() Index([(0, 1), (1, 2)], dtype='object')",
    "markdown_length": 903,
